narrower than twice that), filling of interior holes, the expert additions
(\code{add} polygons and \code{add_sites}), sealing slivers between them
(\code{seal_km}), filling holes again, and finally clipping to \code{extent}, removing
\code{exclude} and trimming to \code{land}.

\strong{Expert intervention.} Everything automatic can be overridden: set
\code{link_km} by hand, add polygons drawn in a GIS (e.g. a valley or migration
route the automatic M leaves out) with \code{add}, add sites known from the
literature with \code{add_sites}, and remove areas with \code{exclude}. The report
states how much area each addition contributes, so it can be reported as
expert-based in the Methods.

